A hint is renamed into place without its fdatasync. The rename's directory
sync can then persist the name over contents a power cut loses: a hint that
fails its CRC, rebuilt by a scan that skips a hint-less file's tail handling,
and open refuses a torn tail it would otherwise have cut.
Guarded-by: "*hint_sync_fails*"

